{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'mechanism draws findings|Small first' ../../../AGENTS.md; rg -n 'Round 32|finite_range|readings_complete|check_p_row|bind_p|bind_rows|gain_credit|pilot_decision' PAID-BUILD.md verdict.py e2e_checks.py; nl -ba PAID-DESIGN.md | sed -n '201,213p'\"","aggregated_output":"85:- When one mechanism draws findings round after round, stop answering findings: propose one structural rule.\n354:- **Small first, then one run.** A hypothesis is first validated the simplest way, on a few stored cases and a few cents, and shown to\ne2e_checks.py:165:            return verdict.pilot_decision(out, str(folder / 'p.json'), str(folder / 'h4.json'), str(folder / 'g.json'), str(key_path), allow_dry=True)\ne2e_checks.py:189:        verdict.pilot_decision(out, str(folder / 'p.json'), str(folder / 'h4.json'), str(folder / 'g.json'), str(key_path))\ne2e_checks.py:225:    credit = verdict.gain_credit(rows, {'d1': (2, 1), 'd2': (3, 1)}, {'d1': (360.0, 360.0), 'd2': (390.0, 390.0)})\nverdict.py:46:def finite_range(low, high):\nverdict.py:50:def readings_complete(fields, key_field):\nverdict.py:60:def check_p_row(row):\nverdict.py:65:    if not readings_complete(fields, 'class'):\nverdict.py:70:    if not finite_range(*s) or not finite_range(*c) or not fields.get('segment excerpt') or not fields.get('company excerpt'):\nverdict.py:77:def bind_p(rows, key, out):\nverdict.py:79:    forecast and reasons), and every row the stores give must be read; each row's reading is then checked (`check_p_row`).\"\"\"\nverdict.py:99:            check_p_row(row)\nverdict.py:241:def gain_credit(gain_rows, gain_dates, segment_ends):\nverdict.py:263:            if fields['cpu increment'] == 'quantified' and not finite_range(fields.get('corrected low'), fields.get('corrected high')):\nverdict.py:283:    return gain_credit([g for g in gain_rows if g['pair'] == n], gain_dates, ends)\nverdict.py:290:def bind_rows(read, expected, content, label):\nverdict.py:303:def pilot_decision(out, p_path, h4_path, gains_path, key_path, allow_dry=False):\nverdict.py:321:    bind_p(p_read, key, out)\nverdict.py:324:    bind_rows(h4, [r for r in worksheet.h_rows(out, 'linked-1', None) if r['part'] == 'H4'], H4_CONTENT, 'H4')\nverdict.py:326:        if r['reader'].get('finding') not in H_FINDINGS['H4'] or not readings_complete(r['reader'], 'finding') or not r['reader'].get('excerpt'):\nverdict.py:346:        bind_rows(gains, expected, GAIN_CONTENT, 'gain review')\nverdict.py:374:    bind_p(p_read, key, out)\nverdict.py:453:        pilot_decision(sys.argv[2], sys.argv[3], sys.argv[4], sys.argv[5], sys.argv[6])\nPAID-BUILD.md:81:   credit from its two supplying answers' reviews (`gain_credit`).\nPAID-BUILD.md:100:  window; mutant `window cut short` caught, `paid-mutant-7.log`); `verdict.bind_p` refuses a P reading that is not exactly the stores'\nPAID-BUILD.md:101:  pairs (a substituted judgement, a shifted span, a missing or duplicated row); `gain_credit` refuses a material failure without its\nPAID-BUILD.md:103:  that date's segment range as read; `verdict.pilot_decision` reads pair 1 alone and cannot give the comparison's pass.\nPAID-BUILD.md:110:## Round 32 findings and the changes (`codex-r32.md`, NOT READY: three)\nPAID-BUILD.md:111:1. **Readings bound to the regenerated rows:** `bind_p` compares each P row's dates and both answers' full forecast and reasons with the\nPAID-BUILD.md:112:   stores' row; `bind_rows` compares each H4 row (request, read judgements shown and their trace, the CPU judgement, control-1's answer\n   201\t## 8. Staged send (D708, council round 31)\n   202\t\n   203\tPair 1 (linked-1, control-1) is registered as pair 1 of this comparison and sent first, its two arms together, on the pinned graph and\n   204\tretirement plan; its stores, archives, snapshots and summaries are kept. Its reading (`worksheet.py build-pilot`, `verdict.py --pilot`):\n   205\tthe blind P rows of both arms read by hand and bound to the stores' pairs; H4 on every post-link v14 answer of linked-1; H1 from the\n   206\tdated summaries; the gain review when the pair is provisionally improved. The pilot's decision, by §4's precedence: a linked double\n   207\trefusal fails; an invalid run, coverage short or control-1 under 2 definite dates is inconclusive; an H1 or H4 harm stops; \"improved\"\n   208\tafter the gain review continues to pairs 2 and 3 and the full reading (pair 1's remaining readings done then under the same rule);\n   209\t\"not improved\" or \"undecided\" stops, each with its reason. The pilot never gives the comparison's pass, which needs three pairs. H3's\n   210\tselector and H5's duplicate counting (round 30) are fixed before the full reading, not before the pilot. Pilot cost about $1.96; the\n   211\tceiling is Alex's (about $2.50 proposed).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
