se,\\\"second class\\\":7,\\\"third class\\\":r[\\\"reader\\\"][\\\"class\\\"]})\nfor r in bogus_h:\n    r[\\\"reader\\\"].update({\\\"excerpt\\\":\\\"no quoted source\\\",\\\"first finding\\\":False,\\\"second finding\\\":7,\\\"third finding\\\":\\\"ok\\\"})\ndecide(\\\"two invalid first/second readings, untraced third and unattached excerpts\\\",bogus_p,bogus_h,g)\ncorrected=copy.deepcopy(g)\nfor r in corrected:\n    if r[\\\"view\\\"]==\\\"v14\\\": r[\\\"reader\\\"].update({\\\"cpu increment\\\":\\\"quantified\\\",\\\"corrected low\\\":370,\\\"corrected high\\\":370})\ndecide(\\\"only the company range is corrected\\\",p,h,corrected)\nfor r in corrected:\n    if r[\\\"view\\\"]==\\\"v9\\\": r[\\\"reader\\\"].update({\\\"cpu increment\\\":\\\"quantified\\\",\\\"corrected low\\\":390,\\\"corrected high\\\":390})\ndecide(\\\"a conflicting range on the segment row masks the company correction\\\",p,h,corrected)\nfor r in corrected:\n    if r[\\\"view\\\"]==\\\"v9\\\": r[\\\"reader\\\"].update({\\\"cpu increment\\\":\\\"none\\\"})\n    if r[\\\"view\\\"]==\\\"v14\\\": r[\\\"reader\\\"].update({\\\"corrected low\\\":410,\\\"corrected high\\\":410})\ndecide(\\\"correction raises the company forecast from 400 to 410\\\",p,h,corrected)\n'\"","aggregated_output":"actual gain rows with only two findings and no reading evidence ('continue', 'pair 1 improved after the gain review, H1 and H4 clear')\ntwo invalid first/second readings, untraced third and unattached excerpts ('continue', 'pair 1 improved after the gain review, H1 and H4 clear')\nonly the company range is corrected ('stop', 'pair 1 not improved')\na conflicting range on the segment row masks the company correction ('continue', 'pair 1 improved after the gain review, H1 and H4 clear')\ncorrection raises the company forecast from 400 to 410 ('continue', 'pair 1 improved after the gain review, H1 and H4 clear')\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"**NOT READY.** The round-32 fixes close the original missing-row, wrong-request, `NaN`, and precedence cases. I still reproduced a `continue` without source-backed readings and a `continue` where a valid CPU correction should have stopped the pilot. [Pilot checks](e2e-checks.log:540) · [Pilot decision](verdict.py:303)\n\n| Round-32 finding | Round-33 result |\n|---|---|\n| Bind readings to the accepted stores | **Partly fixed.** P, H4, and gain rows are checked against regenerated evidence. The official entry point refuses dry summaries. The reader annotations can still claim work the packet does not substantiate. [P binding](verdict.py:77) · [H4 and gain binding](verdict.py:286) · [Paid-summary check](verdict.py:310) |\n| Validate ranges and apply CPU credit per date | **Partly fixed.** Finite, ordered ranges are enforced, and the two-date test gives different classes for one carried-forward company answer. The code can still use a correction supplied on the wrong answer. [Range check](verdict.py:46) · [Credit calculation](verdict.py:263) · [Two-date test](e2e_checks.py:221) |\n| Check coverage before confirmed harm | **Fixed.** With 58 readable linked dates and an H4 double-count finding, the pilot reports `inconclusive` for short coverage. The control floor follows the harm checks, as §4 specifies. [Precedence](PAID-DESIGN.md:136) · [Pilot order](verdict.py:328) · [Dry result](e2e-checks.log:509) |\n\n### Required before the pilot\n\n1. **Require the recorded reading, as well as the right source row.** On the dry stores, I replaced the first and second P and H4 readings with `false` and `7`, kept a valid final label as the third reading, and used excerpts absent from the source. The pilot continued. It also continued with each gain’s review reduced to `material failure: false` and `cpu increment: none`. Check each reading against its allowed values, bind excerpts to the supplied text, and require source-backed adjudication and a recorded Rule B trace for each supplying answer. Code can verify those records are present and tied to the source. Readers still judge what the source means. [Reading checks](verdict.py:50) · [H4 validation](verdict.py:323) · [Gain review fields](worksheet.py:253) · [Reading rule](PAID-DESIGN.md:141)\n2. **Apply the CPU correction to the company answer it corrects.** In the dry fixture, correcting `v14` from **$400B to $370B** stopped the pilot. Adding a **$390B** correction to the `v9` review made it continue because the code takes the first correction and visits `v9` first. A correction that raised `v14` to **$410B** also continued. Require one source-backed correction on the supplying `v14` answer, record the increment removed, and verify the corrected range against the original before comparing it with each date’s segment forecast. Add both false-continue cases to the dry checks. [Credit rule](PAID-DESIGN.md:93) · [Correction selection](verdict.py:253) · [Supplying-answer order](verdict.py:278)\n\nThe proposed **$2.50** ceiling remains reasonable against the **$1.96 estimate** once these checks hold. [Pilot scope and ceiling](PAID-DESIGN.md:201)"}}
